From e75d42771168caaa0b2e7c2e20f2188c77b8409f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Denis Andreyev <257564291+unsound-mint@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:52:47 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] OpenMP in L-BFGS-B: cauchy, subsm, formk, cmprlb, projgr,
 BLAS

With the cost function parallel, about half of the remaining run time
on 12 threads was the serial work of L-BFGS-B on vectors of all n
parameters. These loops now run in parallel in an OPENMP=1 build:

- cauchy: the main loop is split in two passes. The first classifies each
  variable and accumulates f1 and p (parallel); the second builds the
  breakpoint and free-variable lists in index order (serial), so iorder,
  t, nbreak, nfree, ibkmin and bnded are exactly those of the original.
- subsm, cmprlb, formk: the 2m dot products with the correction pairs are
  accumulated in one pass over the free variables (array reductions,
  each sum still in index order), and the per-variable updates run with
  one thread per variable, in the original order of terms.
- projgr: max reduction.
- ddot, dcopy, dscal: long unit-stride vectors in parallel when more than
  one thread is available. All new BLAS lines use the !$ sentinel, so a
  serial build compiles the original code.

In a serial build and with OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 the result is bit-for-bit
the same as before. The hpsolb heap in cauchy, freev and the small 2m x 2m
algebra stay serial.

